# Internationalization

- `html` has a correct `lang` (BCP 47). A fragment in another language has its own `lang`.
- Dates, numbers, currency, phone — via locale, not US-style string glue if the product is not US-only.
- Do not concatenate translation strings (“you have ” + n + “ letters”). Use placeholders and pluralization.
- If the site may be multilingual: logical properties (`margin-inline`, `padding-block`), not hard left/right.
- `dir="rtl"` only for RTL languages. Do not set rtl “just in case”.
- `hreflang` only if real language URLs exist: reciprocal links on each version plus `x-default`. Same annotations in the mobile HTML.
